.TH CHTTPSVR_RESP_WRITE_JSON 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_resp_write_json \- append JSON to the response body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_resp_write_json(chttpsvr_resp *resp,
                                        const char *json, size_t len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Appends len bytes of json to the response body.  It then sets the
Content-Type response header to "application/json".  It writes the
body first.  resp therefore does not change at all when the body
allocation runs out of memory: the function installs no header and
buffers no bytes.

It returns ccol_invalid_args at once, and changes nothing in resp,
when resp or json is NULL, and when len is 0.  A JSON body of zero
length with the Content-Type header set has no valid meaning.  The
function therefore rejects it.  It does not silently set the header
with no body bytes.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - The function appended the body bytes and set
                         the Content-Type header.
ccol_invalid_args      - resp or json is NULL, or len is 0.
ccol_not_enough_memory - The allocation of the body buffer or of the
                         header buffer failed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_set_header (3)
